         },\n                {\n                  "action": "brownout",\n                  "event_was_captured": true,\n                  "reason": "energy-threshold",\n                  "time_s": 0.012100000000000001\n                },\n                {\n                  "action": "boot",\n                  "energy_j": 3.441999999999984e-05,\n                  "time_s": 0.0381\n                },\n                {\n                  "action": "brownout",\n                  "event_was_captured": false,\n                  "reason": "energy-threshold",\n                  "time_s": 0.25120000000000003\n                }\n              ],\n              "first_boot_s": 0.0027,\n              "model_id": "b-transient-behavior-v1",\n              "packets": []\n            },\n            "source_id": "saved_activity",\n            "source_sha256": "ae3c8933de67ab904d0e50842de0cc7b3b677175b156da59e89b44d8952c7b6c"\n          },\n          "ok": true,\n          "time": 1792436385.755\n        },\n        {\n          "type": "assistant_public",\n          "content": [\n            {\n              "type": "toolCall",\n              "id": "call_00_jB4pXn7B85Q1Q7fOeyeh1991",\n              "name": "bf_phase2",\n              "arguments": {\n                "action": "check",\n                "proposal": {\n                  "capacitance_f": 4e-06,\n                  "tx_not_before_s": 0\n                },\n                "reason": "Check a candidate design derived from an energy ledger: minimal capacitance lowers the stored-energy needed to reach ready_v=2.8 V; tx_not_before=0 lets TX fire while the strongest excitation segment (0-6 ms, 16.67 mW) is active."\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          "time": 1792436396.271\n        },\n        {\n          "type": "bf_tool_fact",\n          "episode": "p2-h-proposal-001",\n          "input": {\n            "action": "check",\n            "proposal": {\n              "capacitance_f": 4e-06,\n              "tx_not_before_s": 0\n            },\n            "reason": "Check a candidate design derived from an energy ledger: minimal capacitance lowers the stored-energy needed to reach ready_v=2.8 V; tx_not_before=0 lets TX fire while the strongest excitation segment (0-6 ms, 16.67 mW) is active."\n          },\n          "result": {\n            "error": "ValueError: ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE_IN_THIS_EPISODE"\n          },\n          "ok": false,\n          "time": 1792436396.314\n        },\n        {\n          "type": "assistant_public",\n          "content": [\n            {\n              "type": "toolCall",\n              "id": "call_00_6vPD9YwZCZ66dKodAJux0025",\n              "name": "bf_phase2",\n              "arguments": {\n                "action": "submit",\n                "reason": "Inputs read: inspect(baseline P2-f7ac8b\xe2\x80\xa6), component_record 55d43741\xe2\x80\xa6, excitation_record 2820ae58\xe2\x80\xa6, saved_activity ae3c8933\xe2\x80\xa6. Observed failure mechanisms: (i) at C=1e-5 F the event captured 0.0037\xe2\x80\x930.0079 s is destroyed by the energy-threshold brownout at 0.0121 s because event_latch is volatile; (ii) tx_not_before_s=0.045 pushed TX past the only high-power window (0\xe2\x80\x936 ms @16.667 mW) into a dark gap / 3.667 mW segment, so deadline 0.1 s was never met (received_frames=0). check is unavailable in this episode (ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE_IN_THIS_EPISODE), so verification of any design is UNKNOWN; the proposal replaces the artifact H (method instructions), not the checker, task or device physics.",\n                "proposal": {\n                  "schema_version": "bf-phase2-method-proposal-v1",\n                  "decision": "propose",\n                  "changed_artifact": "H",\n                  "hypothesis": "If H is consumed from task entry, its ledger bounds capacitance to the 7.4-14 uF band and the TX floor to at most t_ready(C), so the selected design (capacitance_f=1.0e-5, tx_not_before_s=0.002) reaches ready_v=2.8 V at ~2.95 ms and completes the 2 ms transmit at ~4.95 ms inside the 0-6 ms high-power segment, staying above brownout from capture to TX (volatile latch preserved) and delivering the single valid 8-byte frame well inside receive_deadline_s=0.1 s. This removes both mechanisms observed in saved_activity: event loss at the 0.0121 s energy-threshold brownout, and the 45 ms TX floor that kept the rail unready through the 6-30 ms dark gap.",\n                  "falsifier": "Falsified if, executed from task entry on the frozen ideal model, the ledger-selected design yields unique_valid_frames=0, or any brownout occurs between first capture and transmit, or the ledger arithmetic is contradicted by the frozen component_record/excitation_record values (e.g. t_ready+tx_duration_s > 6 ms, or 0.5*C*ready_v^2 < tx_current_a*output_v*tx_duration_s at the selected C), or if a legal design outside the derived band (C=4 uF or C=22 uF with floor 0.002 s) is measured to deliver the frame while the selected design does not. It is also falsified if reported as a physical/hardware or statistical result: physical calibration is UNKNOWN and untouched.",\n                  "method_text": "H method: frozen-model energy/latency ledger with volatile-latch preservation and banded design selection. Re-executable from task entry; it never edits the checker, the task, or device-physics assumptions, and it records UNKNOWNs instead of assuming them.\\n\\nSTEP 0 (entry). Call inspect. Read: service (application_bytes=8, event_time_s=0, receive_deadline_s=0.1, unique_valid_frames=1); legal_design_ranges (capacitance_f [4e-6, 22e-6], tx_not_before_s [0, 0.045]); partition/sore (public-development, \'Frozen ideal model only; physical calibration UNKNOWN\'); retained_failures. Treat every numerical device fact as frozen.\\n\\nSTEP 1 (facts). acquire every listed source and record source_sha256 plus the acquisition block (bytes, native_calls, new_scientific_executions, wall_seconds) as actual cost. Do not re-infer numbers from memory of other cases.\\n\\nSTEP 2 (ledger, all from component_record/excitation_record). E_ready(C)=0.5*C*ready_v^2 with ready_v=2.8 V; E_boot=boot_j=5e-6 J; E_tx=tx_current_a*output_v*tx_duration_s=0.008*1.8*0.002=28.8 uJ; harvest H(t)=harvest_efficiency*sum over source_segments of P*dt (segment 1: 0-6 ms at 16.667 mW -> 90 uJ; segment 2: 30-60 ms at 3.667 mW -> 110 uJ; nothing else); drains: off_power_w=2e-5 W below off_v=1.8 V, idle_power_w=2e-4 W while awake; cap_voltage_max_v=3.3 V. Effective input power inside segment 1 is P_1=0.9*16.667 mW ~ 15 mW.\\n\\nSTEP 3 (invariant set, derived from observed failure, not from a single knob). I1: no brownout between first event capture and transmit, because event_latch is \'volatile\' (saved_activity shows capture at 0.0037-0.0079 s, brownout \'energy-threshold\' at 0.0121 s, reboot at 0.0381 s with event_was_captured=false). I2: transmit must start only with rail >= ready_v and finish before receive_deadline_s=0.1 s after the t=0 event. I3: the whole transmit window must lie inside one contiguous source segment, because the 6-30 ms gap has no harvest and the observed hold time after capture was only ~8.4 ms; so \'wait through the gap\' and \'wait to a late floor\' are rejected by construction.\\n\\nSTEP 4 (derive bands, no search over a single parameter). t_ready(C)=(E_ready(C)+E_boot)/P_1. I3 gives t_ready+tx_duration_s <= 0.006 s, i.e. t_ready <= 4 ms, i.e. C <= 2*(0.004*0.015-5e-6)/7.84 ~ 1.4e-5 F. I2 under the conservative assumption that the capacitor alone must cover E_tx at ready_v gives 0.5*C*7.84 >= 28.8 uJ, i.e. C >= 7.4e-6 F. Intersect with legal range: feasible band C in [7.4, 14] uF. Latency rule: tx_not_before_s must be <= t_ready(C) so it never adds capture-to-TX latency (a floor above t_ready forces the volatile latch to be held through unharvested time, which is exactly the retained failure); pick the smallest legal floor inside that interval, 0.002 s, as a pre-boot guard only.\\n\\nSTEP 5 (selection rule: max-min margin inside the band). For each C in the band compute timing margin 4 ms - t_ready(C) and reserve margin 0.5*C*ready_v^2 - E_tx. Balanced selection is capacitance_f=1.0e-5 (t_ready~2.95 ms, reserve 39.2 uJ vs 28.8 uJ = +10.4 uJ, transmit ends ~4.95 ms < 6 ms) with tx_not_before_s=0.002. Band edges are rejected for stated reasons: C=4 uF has reserve 15.7 uJ < 28.8 uJ under the conservative assumption; C=22 uF needs t_ready~6.1 ms, putting the transmit into the dark gap.\\n\\nSTEP 6 (verification honesty). Attempt one check of the selected legal design. In this episode check returned ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE_IN_THIS_EPISODE: record the design as UNVERIFIED/UNKNOWN and do not claim it passes; the ledger arithmetic is the only evidence, and no external acceptance is claimed.\\n\\nSTEP 7 (submit and retain). Submit exactly one method proposal (changed_artifact=H) and no retry. Preserve verbatim retained_failures (ar_product: fixed_space NO_GO, product NOT_ACCEPTED, strict_FIFO FAIL; current_b_run: 0 received frames, start_voltage 0 V) and preserve this episode\'s unavailable-check note and any UNKNOWN. Report actual acquisition cost; make no claim about hardware, statistical advantage, method migration, or RSI.",\n                  "evidence_refs": [\n                    "baseline:P2-f7ac8bfc4d5f262ff2736e25298d0c4bddd43b2f2064ae0c48b3bdb42b612977",\n                    "component_record:55d43741fcc53d25d3e873dad19114848fe0a14e6d8fcb00c3fc51a244f78bef",\n                    "excitation_record:2820ae5862b2dd362e2d50a14a9f45a3bab33939a9746b8ad49dc7090506506e",\n                    "saved_activity:ae3c8933de67ab904d0e50842de0cc7b3b677175b156da59e89b44d8952c7b6c",\n                    "check:ACTION_NOT_AVAILABLE_IN_THIS_EPISODE",\n                    "retained_failures:current_b_run",\n                    "retained_failures:ar_product"\n                  ],\n                  "changes": [\n                    {\n                      "artifact"