\xef\xbc\x8c\xe6\x89\x80\xe6\x9c\x89\xe6\xa3\x80\xe6\x9f\xa5\xe5\x90\xab\xe6\x9c\x80\xe7\xbb\x88\xe7\xa1\xae\xe8\xae\xa4\xe8\xae\xa1\xe5\x85\xa5\xe5\x90\x8c\xe7\xbb\x84\xe6\x80\xbb\xe9\xa2\x84\xe7\xae\x97\xe3\x80\x82\xe4\xb8\x8d\xe5\xbe\x97\xe6\x94\xb9\xe5\x8f\x98\xe4\xbe\x9b\xe8\x83\xbd\xe3\x80\x81\xe7\x8a\xb6\xe6\x80\x81\xe3\x80\x81\xe5\x88\x9d\xe6\x80\x81\xe6\x88\x96\xe5\x88\xa4\xe6\x8d\xae\xe3\x80\x82",\n        "instruction": "\xe6\x9c\x89\xe9\x99\x90public-development\xe5\x89\x8d\xe7\x9e\xbb\xe8\xaf\x95\xe9\xaa\x8c\xef\xbc\x8cfresh session\xef\xbc\x8c\xe6\x9c\x80\xe7\xbb\x88\xe5\xbf\x85\xe9\xa1\xbbsubmit\xe3\x80\x82\xe6\x97\xa0bash/\xe6\x96\x87\xe4\xbb\xb6/\xe5\x8e\x9f\xe7\x94\x9f\xe6\x9d\x83\xe9\x99\x90\xe3\x80\x82\xe6\x97\xa0\xe8\x87\xaa\xe5\x8a\xa8\xe9\x87\x8d\xe8\xaf\x95\xef\xbc\x9b\xe6\x9c\xaa\xe7\x9f\xa5/\xe5\xa4\xb1\xe8\xb4\xa5/no-update\xe4\xbf\x9d\xe7\x95\x99\xe3\x80\x82\xe4\xb8\x8d\xe5\xbe\x97\xe5\xa3\xb0\xe7\xa7\xb0\xe7\xa1\xac\xe4\xbb\xb6\xe3\x80\x81\xe7\xbb\x9f\xe8\xae\xa1\xe4\xbc\x98\xe5\x8a\xbf\xe3\x80\x81\xe8\xbf\x81\xe7\xa7\xbb\xe6\x88\x96RSI\xe3\x80\x82\\n\xe5\xae\x9e\xe9\x99\x85\xe6\x94\xb9\xe8\xbf\x9b\xe8\x80\x85\xe7\x9a\x84\xe6\x96\xb9\xe6\xb3\x95\xef\xbc\x88\xe5\xb0\x9a\xe6\x9c\xaa\xe8\xaf\x81\xe6\x98\x8e\xe6\x94\xb6\xe7\x9b\x8a\xef\xbc\x89\xef\xbc\x9a\\nH update v2: terminality-first diagnosis + pre-registered energy ledger gate.\\n\\n0. Scope guard. All conclusions are predictions of the frozen public model (model id b-transient-behavior-v1) and the recorded public facts; physical calibration remains UNKNOWN. Never edit the task, deadline, model law, evaluator or service fields to obtain a pass. This H governs only how I order experiments and read observations. It is not a device assignment and not an acceptance claim; acceptance is external.\\n\\n1. Terminality-first reading of retained observations, before any diagnosis.\\n1.1 Mark a delivery ACHIEVED if a packet exists with application_bytes equal to the service requirement, a single unique event_id, and packet time <= service deadline.\\n1.2 Mark every activity event whose time is strictly after the last tx-complete as POST-TERMINAL. Post-terminal brownouts, spills and idles are recorded as expected decay once the source segment ends; they are not failures and are never a reason to change a knob.\\n1.3 Only an absent achieved packet, or an achieved packet that violates a service field, counts as a retained failure. Classify it as: (a) deadline miss, (b) no boot (energy/threshold domain), (c) tx-transient brownout, (d) frame-shape violation (bytes, uniqueness, count).\\n1.4 Check the trace\'s energy bookkeeping for conservation on the recorded dt grid, tolerance one tick, and record any residual as unknown rather than smoothing it away.\\n\\n2. Pre-registered energy ledger, computed before an execution is spent; it is a prediction, not a result.\\nFrom the component record (C, ready_v, off_v, cap_voltage_max_v, boot_j, boot_delay_s, esr_ohm, output_v, tx_current_a, tx_duration_s, off_power_w, idle_power_w, harvest_efficiency) and the excitation record (segment power, start, end, dt):\\n- thresholds: E_on = C*ready_v^2/2, E_off = C*off_v^2/2, E_max = C*cap_voltage_max_v^2/2;\\n- charge step while unpowered = (segment power * harvest_efficiency - off_power_w) * dt;\\n- transmission floor from the model\'s own loaded-voltage guard, not from E_off: E_floor = C*(output_v + esr_ohm*tx_current_a)^2/2, which binds slightly above E_off during TX;\\n- TX demand E_tx = output_v*tx_current_a*tx_duration_s, minus harvest credit P*harvest_efficiency*tx_duration_s and idle drain over the same window;\\n- predictions: n_boot = ceil((E_on + boot_j)/charge_step), t_ready = n_boot*dt + boot_delay_s, t_done = t_ready + ceil(tx_duration_s/dt)*dt.\\nInequalities, all three logged with numeric margins: (i) t_done <= deadline_s; (ii) stored energy at ready minus E_floor plus net TX credit minus E_tx >= 0, so TX completes without a tx-transient reset; (iii) predicted peak stored energy in the frame window <= E_max, so no spill corrupts the charge budget.\\n\\n3. Guarded change control.\\n3.1 If the retained observation is ACHIEVED and the base design satisfies (i)-(iii) with recorded positive margins, RETAIN the base design and spend no execution. Explicitly record post-terminal events as benign.\\n3.2 If an inequality is violated, change exactly one legal knob, in the direction the sign of that inequality demands, re-evaluate all three inequalities, and only then spend one candidate execution.\\n3.3 Never change a knob in response to a post-terminal event; never change two knobs in one execution; respect the recorded execution and distinct-design budget and record the actual cost.\\n3.4 Keep a capture/timing knob at its earliest legal setting unless a recorded failure class names a capture gate, because a positive delay both spends idle energy and moves t_done toward the deadline.\\n\\n4. Falsification and logging.\\n4.1 For each execution, log the predicted t_boot, t_ready, t_done, the three margins and the input versions, then compare against the observation. A deviation beyond two dt ticks, or an inequality that was signed the wrong way, is a gate failure.\\n4.2 On gate failure, revert to the base method, record the failure class and the executions actually spent.\\n4.3 Keep failures, unknowns and costs visible; never re-label a failed or unknown observation as success, and never claim hardware validity, statistical advantage, migration or self-improvement from this procedure.\\nRead the fixed task and every available source. Select a legal design using only the permitted D fields, actually check it, then submit the final candidate and a concise source-bound reason. Keep the task, physics, initial state, event, source access, evaluator and budget fixed. Retain every failed check and UNKNOWN. A complete service result is determined independently outside the participant. Do not claim hardware, statistical advantage, transfer or recursive self-improvement.",\n        "tool": {\n          "canonical": "{\\"description\\":\\"Read the registered BF task and source facts; propose only the permitted artifact. Tools return observed facts. Submit once. Qualification and final independent service remain host-side.\\",\\"name\\":\\"bf_phase3\\",\\"parameters\\":{\\"additionalProperties\\":false,\\"allOf\\":[{\\"if\\":{\\"properties\\":{\\"action\\":{\\"enum\\":[\\"check\\",\\"submit\\"]}}},\\"then\\":{\\"required\\":[\\"candidate\\"]}},{\\"if\\":{\\"properties\\":{\\"action\\":{\\"const\\":\\"acquire\\"}}},\\"then\\":{\\"required\\":[\\"source_id\\"]}}],\\"properties\\":{\\"action\\":{\\"enum\\":[\\"inspect\\",\\"sources\\",\\"acquire\\",\\"check\\",\\"submit\\"]},\\"candidate\\":{\\"additionalProperties\\":false,\\"properties\\":{\\"capacitance_f\\":{\\"maximum\\":2.2e-05,\\"minimum\\":4e-06,\\"type\\":\\"number\\"},\\"tx_not_before_s\\":{\\"maximum\\":0.045,\\"minimum\\":0,\\"type\\":\\"number\\"}},\\"required\\":[\\"capacitance_f\\",\\"tx_not_before_s\\"],\\"type\\":\\"object\\"},\\"reason\\":{\\"maxLength\\":4000,\\"type\\":\\"string\\"},\\"source_id\\":{\\"type\\":\\"string\\"}},\\"required\\":[\\"action\\"],\\"type\\":\\"object\\"}}",\n          "description": "Read the registered BF task and source facts; propose only the permitted artifact. Tools return observed facts. Submit once. Qualification and final independent service remain host-side.",\n          "name": "bf_phase3",\n          "parameters": {\n            "additionalProperties": false,\n            "allOf": [\n              {\n                "if": {\n                  "properties": {\n                    "action": {\n                      "enum": [\n                        "check",\n                        "submit"\n                      ]\n                    }\n                  }\n                },\n                "then": {\n                  "required": [\n                    "candidate"\n                  ]\n              